        {
          "id": 401666084,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There's a similar line in other places where preferences are changed via initially loading from the file or via the preferences dialog, but not from Decode As. The Decode As part in QT was refactored quite a bit by Michael Mann three years ago, but even looking in the GTK+ version of the UI I can't see when this used to be called.\n\nI can definitely say that, given the current code, it is broken. See bug #16787 and if you use the TFTP file from #10305 and add the unusual TFTP UDP port via Decode As, global_tftp_port_range ends up pointing to already freed memory. (Since the range_t previously only has a single value, it is freed, and global_tftp_port_range still points to the old freed value instead of getting the new one, since apply_tftp_prefs() is not called before redissection.) This happens in all dissectors, though in most cases it still mostly works, as the Decode As changes are used for the dissector tables, it's only when the preference is used for something else that it can cause issues, like in TFTP how the port is used for conversation tracking (due to how TFTP changes from the static port to two dynamic ports.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
